\lispPackageChapter{livermore/learning-parameters}

The \texttt{livermore/learning-parameters} package holds the numeric knobs for
an XCS run.  Each slot is an accessor on the \texttt{learning-parameters}
class.  The names in quotes below are those used by Butz and
Wilson~\cite{butz-wilson-2002}; the defaults match the values they recommend.

\section{Classes}

\lispClassSubsection{learning-parameters}

An instance of \texttt{learning-parameters} is passed to every XCS.  Only
\texttt{minimum-number-of-actions} has no default; it must be supplied, and is
usually equal to the number of legal actions so that covering can fill any
missing action.

\lispSyntax

\texttt{(make-instance 'learning-parameters :minimum-number-of-actions \lispVar{n} \&key \ldots)}

\lispArgs

\begin{description}
\item[\texttt{maximum-total-numerosity}] $N$ in the paper, usually in the
  hundreds.  Default $100$.
\item[\texttt{learning-rate}] $\beta$, usually in $[0.1, 0.2]$.  Default $0.1$.
\item[\texttt{multiplier-parameter}] $\alpha$, usually $0.1$.  Default $0.1$.
\item[\texttt{equal-error-threshold}] $\epsilon_0$, usually about one percent
  of the reward.  Default $10.0$.
\item[\texttt{power-parameter}] $\nu$, usually $5$.  Default $5$.
\item[\texttt{discount-factor}] $\gamma$, usually $0.71$.  Default $0.71$.
\item[\texttt{ga-threshold}] $\theta_{\mathrm{GA}}$, usually in $[25, 50]$.
  Default $50$.
\item[\texttt{crossover-probability}] $\chi$, usually in $[0.5, 1.0]$.
  Default $0.5$.
\item[\texttt{mutation-probability}] $\mu$, usually in $[0.01, 0.05]$.
  Default $0.025$.
\item[\texttt{deletion-threshold}] $\theta_{\mathrm{del}}$, usually $20$.
  Default $20$.
\item[\texttt{fitness-fraction-threshold}] Used by \texttt{deletion-vote}.
  Default $0.1$.
\item[\texttt{minimum-subsumption-experience}] $\theta_{\mathrm{sub}}$,
  usually at least $20$.  Default $20$.
\item[\texttt{covering-probability}] $P_{\#}$, the chance that a covering
  allele is don't-care.  Default $0.33$.
\item[\texttt{initial-prediction}] $p_I$, slightly more than zero.
  Default $0.001$.
\item[\texttt{initial-prediction-error}] $\epsilon_I$.  Default $0.001$.
\item[\texttt{initial-fitness}] $F_I$.  Default $0.001$.
\item[\texttt{exploration-probability}] $P_{\mathrm{explr}}$.  Default $0.5$.
\item[\texttt{minimum-number-of-actions}] $\theta_{\mathrm{mna}}$.  Required.
\item[\texttt{maximum-number-of-steps}] The cap on a multi-step trial.
  Default $50$.
\item[\texttt{ga-subsumption?}] \texttt{doGASubsumption}.  Default true.
\item[\texttt{action-set-subsumption?}] \texttt{doActionSetSubsumption}.
  Default true.
\item[\texttt{possible-actions}] The legal actions.  Default \texttt{(nil t)}.
\end{description}

\lispExamples

\begin{lstlisting}
(make-instance 'learning-parameters
               :minimum-number-of-actions 2
               :possible-actions '(0 1)
               :maximum-total-numerosity 800)
\end{lstlisting}
